# Gemini API Key for AI features
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Pokee API key for the long-corpus AI lane (/api/ai/pokee → Pokee-Isaac 28B).
# Text-only, 10M-token context, $0.15/$1.00 per Mtok — used for work that needs a
# WHOLE corpus in one prompt (full manuscript, a learner's entire ledger, every
# take's transcript). Claude keeps the creative/persona lane, Gemini the audio +
# vision lane. Get the key at https://console.pokee.ai (format: pk_<tenant>_<token>).
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never give this a VITE_ prefix, that would ship it to browsers.
POKEE_API_KEY=
# Input-token ceiling for /api/ai/pokee. Defaults to 1,000,000 — enough for a whole
# novel or a learner's full ledger, ~$0.15 and ~24s prefill per call. The model can
# take 10M, but that's ~$1.50 and ~73s, so raise this deliberately (max ~6M, where
# the route's 25mb body limit takes over).
POKEE_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=

# Mux API Keys for Video Transcoding and Streaming
MUX_TOKEN_ID=
MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ─── Decentralized Social Layer ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AES-256-GCM key for encrypting Fediverse credentials at rest.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Must be exactly 64 hex characters (32 bytes).
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Public URL of this deployment — used as OAuth redirect base and Mastodon app website.
VITE_APP_URL=https://plajah.com

# ─── Open-access artifact APIs (Archaeology + World History artifact browsers) ──
# Public, read-only, client-side keys for services/artifactsService. The browser
# already works with no keys via The Met, Art Institute of Chicago, Cleveland &
# Open Context (all keyless). These two add the Smithsonian and Europeana:
#
# Smithsonian Open Access (3M+ CC0 objects incl. 3D). Needs a REAL api.data.gov
# key — the shared DEMO_KEY rate-limits too hard for its per-object image fetches,
# so this source stays dormant until a real key is set. Get one free (instant):
# https://api.data.gov/signup/
VITE_SMITHSONIAN_KEY=
# Europeana (58M+ items from Europe's museums/libraries/archives). Free wskey;
# the Europeana source stays dormant until this is set.
# Register (free): https://pro.europeana.eu/pages/get-api
VITE_EUROPEANA_KEY=
# Audius developer-app key (the app ADDRESS — public, safe in the client bundle). Used for
# reads and required for "Log in with Audius". Falls back to the built-in Plajah app key.
# The app's BEARER token is a backend secret and must never appear in a VITE_ var.
# Manage the app (and its redirect URIs) at audius.co → Settings → Developer Apps.
VITE_AUDIUS_API_KEY=

# ─── Admin / Firebase service account ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Service-account JSON (the whole file's contents, single line) used by the
# classics seeder and the /api/admin/seed-classic-books endpoint to upload to
# Firebase Storage. Generate: Firebase console → Project settings →
# Service accounts → Generate new private key.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Shared secret guarding /api/admin/seed-classic-books?key=…
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
ADMIN_SEED_KEY=
# Shared secret guarding /api/cron/publish-due-posts (the Manager Suite scheduled
# publisher). A scheduler (Cloud Scheduler / cron / uptime pinger) calls it each
# minute: POST /api/cron/publish-due-posts?key=<CRON_SECRET>. ADMIN_SEED_KEY also
# works, but a dedicated secret is cleaner. Same generator as above.
CRON_SECRET=

# ─── Firebase App Check (reCAPTCHA v3) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# reCAPTCHA v3 SITE key — public, embedded in the client. Attests that
# Firestore/Storage/Auth traffic comes from the real app. Register the matching
# SITE + SECRET pair in Firebase console → App Check → (this web app) →
# reCAPTCHA v3. The SECRET key lives ONLY in that console form — never here.
VITE_APPCHECK_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# ─── Studio: commercial social networks ────────────────────────────────────────
# Connect-flow credentials for the Manager Suite publish adapters
# (services/socialNetworks). Each network's adapter is built; it activates once
# its app credentials are present and (where noted) the app clears review.
#
# Meta (Instagram + Facebook + Threads) — one app covers all three:
META_APP_ID=
META_APP_SECRET=
# X (Twitter) — OAuth 2.0 app; requires a paid API plan ($200/mo Basic+):
X_CLIENT_ID=
X_CLIENT_SECRET=
# LinkedIn — needs Marketing Developer Platform approval:
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TikTok — needs Content Posting API approval:
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# YouTube uses the Google OAuth client (Google Cloud) + a quota increase:
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── The Post Man: native mail client (Gmail) ──────────────────────────────────
# OAuth client for routes/postman.ts. Each user connects their OWN mailbox; tokens
# are stored per user, per account (users/{uid}/postman_accounts/{accountId}).
# Falls back to GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET when these are unset; with
# neither pair present the API degrades gracefully (GET /api/postman/status returns
# googleConfigured: false and the client hides the Connect button).
#
# Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → the OAuth 2.0 Client ID
# (type: Web application) → "Authorized redirect URIs" → add:
#   https://plajah.com/api/postman/auth/callback
#   http://localhost:8080/api/postman/auth/callback   (local dev; match your port)
# The redirect base comes from VITE_APP_URL, so it must match that host exactly.
# Then APIs & Services → Enabled APIs → enable "Gmail API", and on the OAuth consent
# screen add the scopes: userinfo.email, userinfo.profile, gmail.modify, gmail.send
# (gmail.modify + gmail.send are RESTRICTED scopes — production use needs Google
# verification / a CASA security assessment).
POSTMAN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
POSTMAN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Marketing: Local Reach (billboards + direct mail) ─────────────────────────
# See docs/MARKETING_LOCAL_REACH_SPEC.md. Two very different vendor situations:
#
# Lob — address verification for TARGETED (list-based) direct mail. A genuinely
# public, key-only API (no partner agreement needed) — get a free sandbox key
# (prefix "test_...") at https://dashboard.lob.com/#/settings/api-keys. Used by
# POST /api/marketing/verify-address(-batch). Without it, targeted-mail campaigns
# fall back to the raw uploaded-list count (services/marketing/reachEstimateService
# marks the estimate `source: 'model'` either way — Lob only ever raises the
# CONFIDENCE of that count, never the reach/cost math itself).
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — read as process.env.LOB_API_KEY in server.ts, called only
# from the /api/marketing/verify-address* proxy. Never give this a VITE_ prefix
# or reference it from client code / a vite `define` — that bakes it into the
# shipped bundle in plaintext (see plajah-gemini-key-leak for exactly this class
# of incident with GEMINI_API_KEY).
LOB_API_KEY=
#
# EDDM route/mailbox counts (Taradel) and DOOH screen availability (Adomni/Blip/
# Vistar) are proprietary PARTNER apis — there is no public self-serve key to drop
# in here. Those channels stay on the density-model estimate until a partner
# agreement is signed; do not fabricate calls to these until real credentials and
# a contract exist. Placeholders below so the env shape is ready the day they do:
TARADEL_API_KEY=
DOOH_PARTNER_API_KEY=
